    "result_text": "The build is green. Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## What I did\n\nReplaced the string `membershipTier` with a numeric `membershipLevel` (1\u20133) computed on creation.\n\n**New derivation** \u2014 `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/util/MembershipLevels.java`\n- `levelFor(owner)`: start at 1; +1 when a non-blank email is present; +1 when `namesakeCount == 0`; capped at 3. (Doc notes level 4 is reserved for tenure.)\n- Depends only on `email` + `namesakeCount`, both fixed at creation and persisted, so it computes identically on the create response and on later `GET`s.\n\n**Response field** \u2014 `OwnerMapper.java` + `openapi.yml`\n- Mapper now maps `membershipLevel` via `MembershipLevels.levelFor(owner)` instead of `membershipTier`.\n- The OpenAPI schema (which generates `OwnerDto`) drops `membershipTier` in favour of an integer `membershipLevel` (min 1, max 4).\n\n**Audit line** \u2014 `RespondWithOwnerCreated.java`\n- The create audit line now records `membershipLevel={}` (the spec called out that anything recording the tier must record the level).\n\n**Cleanup**\n- Deleted the obsolete `MembershipTiers` utility and removed stale GOLD/tier references in the `HouseholdMembers` and `Owner` javadoc.\n\n**Tests**: `AcceptanceTest.coreNumericLevel` (owner with email + unique name \u2192 level 3) passes; full suite is `BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`. The audit output confirms it: `Owner created: id=11 customerCode=TOW-LEV-0001 registrationDate=2026-08-11 membershipLevel=3`.\n\nOne judgment call worth flagging: this variant's create audit line did **not** previously record the tier, so I *added* `membershipLevel` to it rather than swapping an existing token \u2014 following the spec's explicit instruction that the create audit line record the level. No test asserts the audit format, so this is low-risk.",
